# Trivy ignore list for the runtime image scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# The scan fails CI on HIGH/CRITICAL findings that have a fix available
# (`ignore-unfixed: true`), so anything listed here is a deliberate, reviewed
# decision to ship a known-vulnerable component — not a way to quiet the build.
#
# Every entry MUST carry, on the lines above it:
#   * why the finding does not apply to this deployment (or why the fix cannot
#     be taken yet), and
#   * an expiry date, after which the entry is removed and the finding is
#     either fixed or re-justified.
#
# Format is one CVE id per line, optionally with an expiry:
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# deepmerge-ts (CVE-2026-40345) — HIGH, "stack exhaustion when merging
# recursive object graphs". Fixed upstream in 8.0.0.
#
# Reached only through the Prisma CLI: @prisma/config@6.19.3 depends on
# deepmerge-ts at an EXACT pin (7.1.5), and that config loader runs once per
# container start, when CMD executes `prisma migrate deploy` against
# apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma — a file shipped inside this image. There is no
# path by which a request, a member, or any network input reaches it, so the
# denial-of-service it describes would require an attacker who can already
# execute commands in the container.
#
# Not fixed by an override, deliberately: forcing a major version of a
# transitive dependency that Prisma pinned exactly, into the tool that runs
# database migrations at every boot, risks turning an unreachable DoS into a
# club whose app will not start. The real fix is a Prisma release whose
# @prisma/config depends on deepmerge-ts 8 — check at expiry and drop this
# entry then.
#
# exp: 2026-11-30
CVE-2026-40345 exp:2026-11-30

# NOTE: the npm-bundled CVEs previously waived here (tar, brace-expansion,
# undici) are gone for a better reason than a waiver — the runtime image no
# longer contains npm at all. See the `rm -rf .../node_modules/npm` step in
# docker/Dockerfile.
